<h2>The game</h2>
<p>Deuteros: The Next Millennium (Activision, 1991) is a space strategy game designed and written by Ian Bird, with graphics by Jai Redman and music by Matt Bates. It is the sequel to Millennium 2.2.</p>
<p>Eight centuries after Millennium, the Earth is habitable again but mankind has lost the way to space. From the Earth base you train producers, researchers and marines, research new technology, build factories and spacecraft, mine the asteroids and settle the Solar System, until you meet the Methanoids and reach for the stars.</p>
<h2>Playing it here</h2>
<p>The game needs Disk 1 and Disk 2 of the original release. It saves to a save disk in drive DF1, which AmigaRecomp keeps for you as a file; the Disks page can load an existing save disk into it.</p>
<p>When the game asks for Disk 2, press F1, open the Disks page and choose Disk 2 for DF0. The Advance Time icon, top left on the main screen, moves time forward; with the hack "Space starts and stops Advance Time" set to modern, as it is by default, Space does the same.</p>
